# cqlite catalog — reads Cassandra SSTables offline via the cqlite_flight Trino
# connector + the cqlite-flight Arrow Flight data plane (one pod per db node).
# Auto-discovered by this kit's own bin/update-catalogs.sh alongside the
# cassandra/clickhouse/opensearch/tidb catalog files, and applied through the
# trino kit's single `helm upgrade`. The catalog is SQL-addressed as
# `cqlite.<keyspace>.<table>`.
#
# ── DEFERRED: connector plugin delivery is blocked on pmcfadin/cqlite#2869 ──
# `cqlite_flight` is a THIRD-PARTY Trino connector (unlike cassandra/clickhouse/
# tidb, which are baked into the stock trinodb/trino image), so this catalog
# only resolves once the connector plugin jar tree is present under
# /usr/lib/trino/plugin/cqlite_flight/ on the coordinator and workers. Until the
# plugin is delivered, registering this catalog makes the coordinator fail at
# boot with "No factory for connector 'cqlite_flight'" — so this file ships as a
# staged template and the plugin-jar delivery is intentionally NOT wired yet.
#
# The earlier approach (a pod-start Gradle initContainer resolving
# in.mcfad:cqlite-trino from Maven Central into an emptyDir) was removed: it is
# being replaced by a single self-contained Shadow fat jar, to be published in
# the cqlite GitHub Releases and tracked in pmcfadin/cqlite#2869. Intended shape
# once #2869 lands:
#   - a versioned per-node hostPath cache (e.g. /var/lib/easydblab/cqlite-plugin/<version>/)
#   - a download-if-missing initContainer that fetches the fat jar from the
#     release URL into that hostPath on first use
#   - nodeSelector: type=app (Trino coordinator/worker node pool)
#   - mount the jar into /usr/lib/trino/plugin/cqlite_flight/ (a SUBDIRECTORY of
#     the plugin path, never the plugin path itself, so image-baked plugins are
#     not shadowed)
# This is Helm-values shaped (initContainer + volumes on coordinator/worker), so
# it will be wired into the trino chart values once the artifact exists. Do NOT
# invent a jar URL or reintroduce a Gradle pod-start resolve here.
#
# connector.name MUST equal the registered Trino connector factory name,
# `cqlite_flight` (CqliteFlightConnectorFactory.getName()); setting it to the
# catalog name `cqlite` crashes the coordinator at boot (issue #2123).
connector.name=cqlite_flight
cqlite.sidecar-uri=__SIDECAR_URI__
cqlite.flight-port=__FLIGHT_PORT__
# Preferred datacenter for split placement. Renders BLANK when not supplied,
# which the connector treats as "no DC preference".
cqlite.local-datacenter=__LOCAL_DATACENTER__
# How each scan resolves the SSTable file set: snapshot (consistent per-query
# Sidecar snapshot) | live (current data dir, races compaction).
cqlite.read-mode=__READ_MODE__
